CAT = "melecLoadCalc"; SEG = "LOD"
Q = [
("Standard method, 120/240 V dwelling: 2,200 sq ft, two small-appliance and one laundry circuit, 12 kW range, 5.5 kW dryer, four fastened appliances totaling 8.2 kW, 10 kW heat and 6 kVA A/C. About what is the calculated load?",
 "About 148 A", ["About 131 A", "About 156 A", "About 165 A"],
 "Lighting and circuits 11,100 VA demand to 5,835; range 8,000; dryer 5,500; appliances 8,200 x 0.75 = 6,150; heat 10,000 (the larger noncoincident load). Total 35,485 VA / 240 V is about 148 A. Counting the A/C instead of the heat gives 131 A."),
("In the standard calculation, what demand load is used for one 15 kW household range?",
 "9.2 kW", ["8.0 kW", "12.0 kW", "11.25 kW"],
 "Column C allows 8 kW for one range up to 12 kW. Note 1 adds 5 percent for each kW above 12: 3 kW over is 15 percent, and 8 x 1.15 = 9.2 kW."),
("Three 12 kW household ranges supplied by one feeder have what Column C demand?",
 "14 kW", ["36 kW", "24 kW", "27 kW"],
 "Column C of the range demand table gives 14 kW for three ranges rated not over 12 kW each. Taking 8 kW per range, 24 kW, ignores the diversity the table allows."),
("A 6 kW counter-mounted cooktop and two 4 kW wall ovens are in one kitchen. Treated as one range, what is their demand load?",
 "8.8 kW", ["14 kW", "8.0 kW", "11.2 kW"],
 "A cooktop and up to two wall ovens in the same room may be added together and treated as one range: 14 kW is 2 kW over 12, so Column C's 8 kW rises 10 percent to 8.8 kW."),
("A household range has an 8 kW demand load. What neutral load may be used for it in the service calculation?",
 "5.6 kW", ["8.0 kW", "4.0 kW", "6.4 kW"],
 "The feeder or service neutral load for household ranges, ovens, cooktops and dryers may be taken at 70 percent of their demand: 8 x 0.70 = 5.6 kW."),
("Six 5 kW electric clothes dryers in an apartment building are calculated by the standard method. What is their demand load?",
 "22.5 kW", ["25.5 kW", "30 kW", "19.5 kW"],
 "The dryer demand table allows 75 percent for six dryers: 30 kW x 0.75 = 22.5 kW. Five dryers would be 85 percent and seven 65 percent."),
("A dwelling has 9 kW of electric heat and a 7.5 kVA air conditioner that never run together. In the standard calculation, which is included?",
 "The 9 kW heat only", ["Both loads in full", "The A/C load only", "Half of each load"],
 "Noncoincident loads that will not run at the same time may be counted by using only the larger one. Here the 9 kW heat is larger than the 7.5 kVA A/C."),
("A 120/240 V service has a calculated unbalanced neutral load of 320 A, all linear. What neutral load may be used?",
 "284 A", ["320 A", "224 A", "260 A"],
 "The first 200 A of neutral load is taken at 100 percent and the part over 200 A at 70 percent: 200 + (120 x 0.70) = 284 A."),
("Optional method, one dwelling: the general loads other than heating and A/C total 40 kVA. What demand is taken for them?",
 "22 kVA", ["16 kVA", "25 kVA", "40 kVA"],
 "The optional method counts the first 10 kVA of general load at 100 percent and the rest at 40 percent: 10 + (30 x 0.40) = 22 kVA."),
("Optional method: a dwelling has 15 kW of central electric heat and a 7 kVA air conditioner. What heating and cooling load is used?",
 "9.75 kVA", ["15 kVA", "7 kVA", "16.75 kVA"],
 "The optional method takes the largest of the A/C at 100 percent and central electric space heat at 65 percent. 15 x 0.65 = 9.75 kVA, which is more than the 7 kVA A/C."),
("Optional method: a dwelling heats with five separately controlled room heaters. At what percent is their nameplate load taken?",
 "40 percent", ["65 percent", "75 percent", "100 percent"],
 "Four or more separately controlled electric space heating units are taken at 40 percent of nameplate. Fewer than four, or central heat, are taken at 65 percent."),
("An existing dwelling with no new heating or A/C has a total load of 30 kVA by the existing-dwelling optional method. What is the demand?",
 "16.8 kVA", ["18.8 kVA", "12 kVA", "30 kVA"],
 "For an existing dwelling adding no heating or air conditioning, the first 8 kVA is taken at 100 percent and the rest at 40 percent: 8 + (22 x 0.40) = 16.8 kVA."),
("Optional method for a 20-unit building, each unit calculated at 22 kVA. What is the total demand?",
 "167.2 kVA", ["154 kVA", "171.6 kVA", "440 kVA"],
 "The multifamily optional table gives 38 percent for 18 to 20 units: 20 x 22 kVA = 440 kVA, and 440 x 0.38 = 167.2 kVA."),
("For the multifamily optional calculation, each dwelling unit must have electric space heating or air conditioning and:",
 "Electric cooking", ["Gas water heating", "A separate service", "A laundry circuit"],
 "The optional multifamily method applies only when no unit is fed by more than one feeder, each unit has electric cooking equipment, and each has electric heat, A/C or both."),
("A restaurant has five kitchen units totaling 60 kW; the two largest are 15 kW and 12 kW. What is the feeder demand?",
 "42 kW", ["39 kW", "48 kW", "60 kW"],
 "The commercial kitchen table allows 70 percent for five units: 60 x 0.70 = 42 kW. That is more than the 27 kW of the two largest, so 42 kW is used."),
("Four commercial kitchen units are rated 20, 18, 3 and 2 kW. What demand load must be used?",
 "38 kW", ["34.4 kW", "43 kW", "30.1 kW"],
 "Four units at 80 percent give 34.4 kW, but the demand may never be less than the two largest units together, 20 + 18 = 38 kW."),
("An office has 120 general-use receptacles counted at 180 VA each. What receptacle demand load is used?",
 "15,800 VA", ["21,600 VA", "10,800 VA", "16,200 VA"],
 "120 x 180 = 21,600 VA. Nondwelling receptacle loads take the first 10 kVA at 100 percent and the rest at 50 percent: 10,000 + 5,800 = 15,800 VA."),
("A store has 30 ft of show window. What minimum load is calculated for it?",
 "6,000 VA", ["3,600 VA", "5,400 VA", "1,200 VA"],
 "Show-window lighting is figured at 200 VA per linear foot of window, measured horizontally along its base: 30 x 200 = 6,000 VA."),
("A store has 40 ft of multioutlet assembly where appliances are not likely to be used at the same time. What load is calculated?",
 "1,440 VA", ["7,200 VA", "2,880 VA", "1,800 VA"],
 "Each 5 ft of multioutlet assembly counts as 180 VA where appliances are unlikely to be used together: 40 / 5 = 8 sections x 180 = 1,440 VA."),
("In a 2023 NEC dwelling calculation, a 6 kW electric vehicle supply equipment unit is counted at:",
 "7,200 W", ["6,000 W", "7,500 W", "9,600 W"],
 "Article 220 counts EV supply equipment at 7,200 W or its nameplate rating, whichever is larger. A 6 kW unit is therefore counted at 7,200 W."),
("A year of demand data shows a building's highest demand was 160 A. For adding new load, the existing load is taken as:",
 "200 A", ["160 A", "176 A", "240 A"],
 "When existing load is found from a year of maximum demand data, it is taken at 125 percent: 160 x 1.25 = 200 A, and the new load is added to that."),
("A commercial building has two tenant entrances, each needing a sign outlet. What minimum sign load is calculated?",
 "2,400 VA", ["1,200 VA", "3,600 VA", "2,000 VA"],
 "Each required sign outlet is calculated at no less than 1,200 VA, and one is required at each entrance to each tenant space: 2 x 1,200 = 2,400 VA."),
("A commercial building's calculated load is 180 kVA at 208Y/120 V three-phase. About what service current does this require?",
 "About 500 A", ["About 865 A", "About 289 A", "About 375 A"],
 "Three-phase current is VA / (V x 1.732): 180,000 / (208 x 1.732) is about 500 A. Dividing by 208 alone gives 865 A."),
("A dwelling has only three fastened-in-place appliances besides the range, dryer and HVAC. At what percent are they counted?",
 "100 percent", ["75 percent", "125 percent", "65 percent"],
 "The 75 percent demand factor applies only to four or more fastened-in-place appliances on the same feeder or service. With three, they count at 100 percent of nameplate."),
]
